# EC2 Auto Scaling Project (Free Tier Friendly – us-east-1)

## Set Region

```bash
aws configure set region us-east-1
```

---

# 1. Create Launch Template

## Get Latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI

```bash
aws ssm get-parameters \
--names /aws/service/ami-amazon-linux-latest/amzn2-ami-hvm-x86_64-gp2
```

Copy the `Value` (AMI ID).

---

## Create Security Group

```bash
aws ec2 create-security-group \
--group-name free-asg-sg \
--description "Free Tier ASG Security Group" \
--vpc-id YOUR_VPC_ID
```

---

## Allow HTTP

```bash
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
--group-name free-asg-sg \
--protocol tcp \
--port 80 \
--cidr 0.0.0.0/0
```

---

## Create Launch Template

```bash
aws ec2 create-launch-template \
--launch-template-name free-tier-template \
--version-description v1 \
--launch-template-data '{
  "ImageId":"AMI_ID",
  "InstanceType":"t2.micro",
  "SecurityGroupIds":["SG_ID"],
  "UserData":"IyEvYmluL2Jhc2gKeXVtIHVwZGF0ZSAteQp5dW0gaW5zdGFsbCAteSBodHRwZApzeXN0ZW1jdGwgc3RhcnQgaHR0cGQKc3lzdGVtY3RsIGVuYWJsZSBodHRwZAplY2hvICJIZWxsbyBmcm9tIEF1dG8gU2NhbGluZyIgPiAvdmFyL3d3dy9odG1sL2luZGV4Lmh0bWw="
}'
```

---

# 2. Create Auto Scaling Group

```bash
aws autoscaling create-auto-scaling-group \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--launch-template LaunchTemplateName=free-tier-template,Version=1 \
--min-size 1 \
--max-size 2 \
--desired-capacity 1 \
--vpc-zone-identifier "SUBNET_ID_1,SUBNET_ID_2" \
--health-check-type EC2 \
--health-check-grace-period 300
```

> Free tier safe values:

* Min = 1
* Desired = 1
* Max = 2

---

# 3. Manual Scaling

## Scale Up

```bash
aws autoscaling update-auto-scaling-group \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--desired-capacity 2
```

---

## Scale Down

```bash
aws autoscaling update-auto-scaling-group \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--desired-capacity 1
```

---

# 4. Scheduled Scaling

## Scale Up Morning

```bash
aws autoscaling put-scheduled-update-group-action \
--scheduled-action-name morning-scale-up \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--recurrence "0 4 * * 1-5" \
--min-size 1 \
--max-size 2 \
--desired-capacity 2
```

---

## Scale Down Evening

```bash
aws autoscaling put-scheduled-update-group-action \
--scheduled-action-name evening-scale-down \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--recurrence "0 14 * * 1-5" \
--min-size 1 \
--max-size 2 \
--desired-capacity 1
```

---

# 5. Simple Scaling Policy

## Create CloudWatch Alarm

```bash
aws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm \
--alarm-name high-cpu-alarm \
--metric-name CPUUtilization \
--namespace AWS/EC2 \
--statistic Average \
--period 300 \
--threshold 70 \
--comparison-operator GreaterThanThreshold \
--dimensions Name=AutoScalingGroupName,Value=free-tier-asg \
--evaluation-periods 2 \
--alarm-actions SCALE_POLICY_ARN
```

---

## Create Simple Scaling Policy

```bash
aws autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--policy-name simple-scale-up \
--scaling-adjustment 1 \
--adjustment-type ChangeInCapacity \
--cooldown 300
```

---

# 6. Step Scaling Policy

## Create Step Scaling Policy

```bash
aws autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--policy-name step-scale-policy \
--policy-type StepScaling \
--step-adjustments MetricIntervalLowerBound=0,ScalingAdjustment=1 \
--adjustment-type ChangeInCapacity
```

---

# 7. Target Tracking Scaling

```bash
aws autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--policy-name target-tracking-policy \
--policy-type TargetTrackingScaling \
--target-tracking-configuration '{
  "PredefinedMetricSpecification":{
    "PredefinedMetricType":"ASGAverageCPUUtilization"
  },
  "TargetValue":50.0
}'
```

---

# 8. Predictive Scaling (Optional)

⚠ Predictive scaling may create additional resources and can exceed free tier.

```bash
aws autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
--policy-name predictive-policy \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--policy-type PredictiveScaling \
--predictive-scaling-configuration '{
  "MetricSpecifications":[
    {
      "TargetValue":50.0,
      "PredefinedMetricPairSpecification":{
        "PredefinedMetricType":"ASGCPUUtilization"
      }
    }
  ],
  "Mode":"ForecastOnly"
}'
```

Use:

* `ForecastOnly` → safer for free tier
* Avoid `ForecastAndScale`

---

# 9. Instance Refresh

## Create New Launch Template Version

```bash
aws ec2 create-launch-template-version \
--launch-template-name free-tier-template \
--source-version 1 \
--version-description v2
```

---

## Start Instance Refresh

```bash
aws autoscaling start-instance-refresh \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--strategy Rolling \
--preferences '{
  "MinHealthyPercentage":50,
  "InstanceWarmup":120
}'
```

---

## Check Refresh Status

```bash
aws autoscaling describe-instance-refreshes \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg
```

---

# 10. Warm Pool (Optional)

⚠ Warm pools keep stopped instances and may incur EBS charges.

```bash
aws autoscaling put-warm-pool \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--pool-state Stopped \
--min-size 1 \
--max-group-prepared-capacity 2
```

---

# 11. View Auto Scaling Group

```bash
aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups \
--auto-scaling-group-names free-tier-asg
```

---

# 12. Delete Resources (Avoid Charges)

## Delete ASG

```bash
aws autoscaling delete-auto-scaling-group \
--auto-scaling-group-name free-tier-asg \
--force-delete
```

---

## Delete Launch Template

```bash
aws ec2 delete-launch-template \
--launch-template-name free-tier-template
```

---

# Free Tier Recommendations

| Resource           | Recommended  |
| ------------------ | ------------ |
| Instance Type      | t2.micro     |
| Desired Capacity   | 1            |
| Max Capacity       | 2            |
| Predictive Scaling | ForecastOnly |
| Warm Pool          | Optional     |
| Region             | us-east-1    |

